<IndexLayout title="About">
  <p>In 2026 summer, I graduated with a bachelor's degree in physics from Yan Jici Elite Class in USTC. Currently I'm working in Prof. Hongtao Yang's group at USTC, applying for PhD program for 2027 Fall.</p>
  <section class="template-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 / Background</p>
    <div>
      <h2>An Odyssey of Research</h2>
      <p>My research interests began in fundamental physics, for which I participated in search for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons in 2023 winter under the supervision of Prof. Nan Lu at USTC. This project lasted for nearly 2 years, and in 2025 summer I flew to CERN to further conduct this analysis in collaboration with Caltech's group under the supervision of Prof. Si Xie at Fermilab.</p>
      <p>Such physics analysis could be important to deepen our understanding of the Higgs coupling with fermions, but personally, my interest was drawn by machine learning in this work. In addition, I want to explore some innovation beyond fundamental physics. Therefore, I also participated in some projects like a workload profiling of Neural Network Variational Monte Carlo, and a Multi-Agent System development. Also, I served as the student helper in ICML AI4S workshop 2026. These experiences broaden my horizon in this era of AI storm.</p>
      <p>However, after such an Odyssey of research path, my interest still lies in the field of fundamental physics, but with a particular interest of AI-enhanced methodology development. From 2026 summer, I work as a research assistant in Prof. Hongtao Yang's group at USTC, studying the post-refinement of multi-task jet tagging model in collaboration with Prof. Bingxuan Liu in SYSU, as my first step back in the intersection of particle physics and AI/ML.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="template-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 / Lifetime</p>
    <div>
      <h2>Once upon a Time...</h2>
      <p>Before entering the University, I grew up in Zhongshan, a small city in the South of China.</p>
      <p>My interest in fundamental physics was sparked at an early age, when I first read the rules of our world from the books. Romanticism and nihilism are also key motivations for me beyond the pursuit of scientific knowledge, where physics gives me a feeling of connection to the universe. Like many people viewing the world in this way, I'm interested in philosophy and humanities.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="template-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 / Elsewhere</p>
    <div>
      <h2>Outside the Desk.</h2>
      <p>Started from my first day at USTC, I joined the USTC Martial Arts Association, where I mainly practiced Kick-Boxing and traditional Chinese staff techniques. And I also made some close friends within this club, which enriched my university life significantly. In 2024 summer, I was elected as the president of the USTC Martial Arts Association. Not only did I enlarge the scale of the association 2-fold, but I also organized 1st USTC Martial Arts Tournament and 2nd USTC Wushu Exchange Conference among Hefei universities. This experience greatly enhanced my leadership and organizational skills.</p>
      <p>More to be added in the future.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
